# =============================================================================
# RemoteRecruit — root (frontend) environment template
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your values. `.env` is gitignored.
# =============================================================================

# Backend API base URL used by the client (see src/api/client.js).
# - In local development, omit this (or leave empty): the Vite dev server
#   proxies /api -> http://localhost:5000, so the default "/api" works.
# - When the frontend and the API are deployed on SEPARATE domains, set this
#   to the full backend URL INCLUDING the /api prefix, e.g.
#       VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend.vercel.app/api
# - When they share one domain (frontend + API on the same Vercel project),
#   omit it — relative "/api" already hits the same-domain backend.
#
# NOTE for Vercel: Vite variables are baked in at BUILD time and a local
# `.env` file is gitignored (never uploaded). To configure the deployed site,
# add VITE_API_URL in Vercel -> Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables,
# then redeploy. A local `.env` only affects local development.
#
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend.vercel.app/api
